  "expectedDraftMasterHash": "sha256:9f6ff2520401b955c3ae77ce52da6a57ecf64750a10710729736d4dea616b248",
  "visualBrief": "The Isetan and Granvia wings flank an open atrium under a curved steel and glass canopy. The Grand Staircase rises 35 metres to the west terrace, with a suspended Skyway and tiered galleries above the entrance hall. The Hachijō frontage encloses the raised Shinkansen decks and connects to the mapped platform sheds.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 34 m sea-level datum is taken from standard viewer terrain. Karasuma and Hachijō floors fit the open approach samples. Separate terrain and pavement masks seat the north wings, atrium and station rail floors where the standard terrain samples rise over the built footprint.",
  "nativeAxes": "The longest Karasuma frontage sets the signed +X axis toward the east wing. The named station stops and Hachijō Street distinguish the north plaza from the south rail terminal.",
  "limitations": [
    "The podium, outer building wings, rail centerlines and platform shelter footprints follow PMTiles. Photo interpretation supplies the atrium section, public circulation and individual facade bays.",
    "The forecourt elevations follow open Terrarium approach samples. The station floors and railway deck elevations are reconstructed to bridge high samples over the built site.",
    "The model represents the exterior, the public atrium and the above-ground track concourses. Stairs, escalators and railway fixtures are static geometry."
  ],
